{"metadata":{"kernelspec":{"display_name":"Python 3","language":"python","name":"python3"},"language_info":{"name":"python","version":"3.12.13","mimetype":"text/x-python","codemirror_mode":{"name":"ipython","version":3},"pygments_lexer":"ipython3","nbconvert_exporter":"python","file_extension":".py"}},"nbformat_minor":5,"nbformat":4,"cells":[{"id":"599df0bc-68ae-44ae-a174-e930bd736b32","cell_type":"markdown","source":"# Week 8 — Gradient Boosting II: LightGBM + SHAP + Model Stacking\n**Date:** July 28, 2026\n**Week:** 8 of 10 — follows Week 7 (XGBoost, closed out; SHAP explicitly deferred to this week)\n\nXGBoost edged out RF as your best single model this week just closed, but by a thin margin, and RF's two weak spots (`class_target_2`, `class_target_3_corrected` LONG) got closed rather than blown open — worth keeping in mind before this week's tools invite overconfidence. This week has four real jobs, in order: (1) finally compile the RF-vs-XGBoost win/loss tally Week 7 never assembled, so \"current best\" means something concrete; (2) add LightGBM as a third tree ensemble and run SHAP across all three models together — the interpretability pass Week 7 deliberately postponed rather than redoing later; (3) build a stacking ensemble to see whether combining model families beats any single one; (4) do a genuine mid-point review of every model trained since Week 1, plus a first look at regime-dependence (trending vs ranging markets). None of this is a free pass to treat this week's numbers as more solid than last week's — SHAP agreement, stacking gains, and regime splits are all new places for optimistic bias to hide if you don't check for it the same way you checked Week 4's `class_target_3`.\n","metadata":{}},{"id":"063c3e2b-ded5-4094-b325-30ce6f44427b","cell_type":"markdown","source":"---","metadata":{}},{"id":"bdb88f6e-dfea-442e-a99e-35ddccdea54f","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## PART A — Setup (carried forward from Week 7, complete)","metadata":{}},{"id":"a6c3d8b5-ad94-433b-85dd-57d378c3e74a","cell_type":"markdown","source":"### A.0 — Carrying Week 7's lessons forward, explicitly\n\nTwo of these bit you again *inside* Week 7 itself, after being named as fixed — read this before writing anything below.\n\n1. **`RESULTS_DIR`/`save_result_dict` shadowing recurred in Week 7's own Optuna tuning cells** (both classification and regression), *after* being named a standing rule earlier the same week. Both are defined once, in A.9 below. No downstream cell — tuning sweep, comparison table, anything copy-pasted from a prior cell or a prior week — should reassign `RESULTS_DIR = 'results'` or redefine `save_result_dict` locally. If you're about to paste a sweep cell from Week 7, check this first.\n2. **Git identity must be configured at the top of *this* session, not assumed carried over.** Week 7 hit `fatal: unable to auto-detect email address` again at close-out, on a fresh container, despite this being written up as a Week 7 fix already. Run A.9's identity cell before anything that calls `save_progress()`.\n3. **Any Optuna study over ~15 minutes uses persistent `storage=sqlite:///...`, not in-memory.** Week 7's 50-trial regression sweep ran close to 90 minutes in-memory; if a Kaggle session had died mid-sweep, all of it would have been lost.\n4. **If you narrow a hyperparameter search space around a previous round's best trial, say so explicitly in the record** — Week 7's round 2 measured local refinement around round 1's single best trial, not independent re-exploration. Don't report it as if it were a broader search.\n5. **Diff any fully-regenerated setup cell against the previous verified version before running it.** Week 7 lost `target_exit` this way once already.\n6. **Log1p A/B tests must pass the *string* transform key (`'log1p'`/`'log5p'`), not a bare `True`/`False`.** `cv_regression()`'s offset lookup is keyed on the string, so passing a boolean silently resolves to \"no transform\" on both sides of a comparison — a same-vs-same test that can't detect anything, even though it will still print numbers. Sanity-check any A/B cell you write below by confirming the \"no transform\" and \"with transform\" runs actually produce different R² before trusting the delta.\n","metadata":{}},{"id":"749577f6-c662-494b-8dd7-2123ca3c71f6","cell_type":"markdown","source":"### A.0.1 — Standing checks from `ADVICE.md` (re-run this pulse-check every week, not just at Week 11)\n\nThese aren't this week's main topic, but skipping them silently is exactly the pattern `ADVICE.md` was written to stop. Answer briefly before treating anything below as a \"win\":\n- Is the CV-leakage question (early-stopping slice overlapping the last walk-forward fold) still deferred? It was deferred once in Week 7 for RF/XGBoost comparability. If LightGBM's baseline this week inherits the same simplification, say so explicitly — don't let it quietly become a fourth week of \"comparable, but not rigorous.\"\n- Do you have even a rough \"would this have made money\" number yet for your current best model? Not required to be exact — a naive PnL-if-every-flagged-signal-was-taken number is enough to keep the actual goal in view.\n- Any target being leaned on as a leaderboard leader — is it still worth re-checking against the volatility-ablation pattern that caught `class_target_3_corrected`?\n","metadata":{}},{"id":"0aeccfb6-abbf-4498-9e53-ae82e4b85f66","cell_type":"code","source":"# TODO: write 2-4 sentences per bullet above, based on this week's actual state --\n# not a restatement of last week's answer. If nothing has changed, say so explicitly\n# rather than leaving it blank.\nadvice_pulse_check = \"\"\"\nCV leakage status: ...\nRough PnL-if-taken number for current best model: ...\nAny leaderboard leader worth re-ablating: ...\n\"\"\"\nprint(advice_pulse_check)\n","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"id":"d3cbb569-aae8-4e26-904c-eeb84f77514f","cell_type":"markdown","source":"---","metadata":{}},{"id":"5da91b7f-bd39-402b-b40d-74c5828f70f6","cell_type":"markdown","source":"### A.1 — Install packages","metadata":{}},{"id":"3fee1913-deba-43a7-ac50-1bd8f232881f","cell_type":"code","source":"!pip install -q supabase scikit-learn statsmodels xgboost lightgbm shap optuna\n","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"id":"1d382027-e76e-4b62-b49f-ac3be7cb5c67","cell_type":"markdown","source":"### A.2 — Environment detection + secrets (Kaggle-primary, Colab-compatible)","metadata":{}},{"id":"b8587477-78d9-4cfa-94c8-2af14a69dfbe","cell_type":"code","source":"import os\n\nIS_KAGGLE = 'KAGGLE_KERNEL_RUN_TYPE' in os.environ\nIS_COLAB = 'COLAB_RELEASE_TAG' in os.environ\n\nif IS_KAGGLE:\n    from kaggle_secrets import UserSecretsClient\n    secrets = UserSecretsClient()\n    get_secret = lambda k: secrets.get_secret(k).strip()\nelif IS_COLAB:\n    from google.colab import userdata\n    get_secret = lambda k: userdata.get(k)\nelse:\n    # local/other -- read from os.environ as a fallback\n    get_secret = lambda k: os.environ[k]\n\nprint(f\"Environment: {'Kaggle' if IS_KAGGLE else 'Colab' if IS_COLAB else 'Other/local'}\")\n# Do NOT unconditionally import google.colab.userdata below this cell \"just in case\" --\n# Week 7 carried a dead Colab import into a Kaggle session. Branch, don't duplicate.\n","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"id":"1197d555-04a5-4c98-b429-bbe978a1901a","cell_type":"markdown","source":"### A.3 — Git identity (set BEFORE anything calls save_progress, every session)","metadata":{}},{"id":"48d81ee9-c889-46a0-95aa-78c3f52a9583","cell_type":"code","source":"import subprocess\n\nUSER_EMAIL       = \"israelbajulaye@student.oauife.edu.ng\"\nGITHUB_USERNAME  = \"Jeshurun-B\"\n\n# TODO: run these two lines every session, unconditionally -- do not assume a fresh\n# container inherited a previous session's git identity.\nsubprocess.run([\"git\", \"config\", \"--global\", \"user.email\", USER_EMAIL], check=True)\nsubprocess.run([\"git\", \"config\", \"--global\", \"user.name\", GITHUB_USERNAME], check=True)\n","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"id":"cd10746d-49f9-49c9-86eb-6e02455b23a6","cell_type":"markdown","source":"### A.4 — Connect to both databases","metadata":{}},{"id":"a58cf761-6d2c-4b93-891a-5d4bdf96442f","cell_type":"code","source":"import pandas as pd\nimport numpy as np\nfrom supabase import create_client\n\n# Main DB\nmain_client = create_client(get_secret('SUPABASE_URL'), get_secret('SUPABASE_KEY'))\n\n# Analytics DB\nanalytics_client = create_client(get_secret('ANALYTICS_SUPABASE_URL'), get_secret('ANALYTICS_SUPABASE_KEY'))\n\nprint(\"Connected to both Supabase projects.\")\n","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"id":"63efc347-6436-4639-9194-7cbe02f05b45","cell_type":"markdown","source":"### A.5 — Fetch + merge (keep exactly one merged dataframe)","metadata":{}},{"id":"baa3c072-4140-47ca-b5d9-25be18388def","cell_type":"code","source":"# TODO: fetch df_main from 'signals' (status == 'analyzed'), df_analytics from 'crossover_analytics'\n# TODO: rename df_analytics 'crossover_utc' -> 'checked_at_utc'\n# TODO: inner-merge on ['checked_at_utc', 'symbol'] into ONE dataframe named df -- do not\n#       also keep a second parallel dataframe around (Week 3's df/df_all mistake)\n# TODO: print(f\"Merged: {len(df):,} rows | {df.shape[1]} columns\")\ndf = None  # placeholder\n","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"id":"0df67608-8321-48e0-a66d-ea5b9d9335a6","cell_type":"markdown","source":"### A.6 — Targets: classification + regression (carried forward, unchanged from Week 7)\nRetired: the old T1–T4 / `target_special` system and `class_target_3`. Do not regenerate either.\n\n**`REG_TARGETS` format note (changed mid-Week-7):** the transform flag is now a *string* (`'log1p'`, `'log5p'`, or `'none'`/absent), not a boolean. `quality`'s `log5p` (ln(y+5) + Duan's smearing) was confirmed merged into `cv_regression()` this week — carry the string-keyed version forward, not the old boolean version from the Week 5/6 session prompt.","metadata":{}},{"id":"71059459-2329-4181-8e1d-cde736f20897","cell_type":"code","source":"def optimal_entry_candle(row):\n    \"\"\"Returns 15-min candles from crossover to optimal entry. 0 = immediate entry.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        if pd.isnull(row['optimal_entry_utc']) or pd.isnull(row['checked_at_utc']):\n            return 0.0\n        return float((row['optimal_entry_utc'] - row['checked_at_utc']).total_seconds() / 900)\n    except Exception:\n        return 0.0\n\n# TODO: df['Optimum_entry'] = df.apply(optimal_entry_candle, axis=1)\n\n# --- Classification targets ---\n# TODO: mae_abs, mfe_abs = df['mae_percent'].abs(), df['mfe_percent'].abs()\n# TODO: df['target_b'] = (mfe_abs / (mfe_abs + mae_abs + 1e-8)) * (mfe_abs - mae_abs)\n# TODO: df['class_target_1'] = (df['target_b'] > 0.4).astype(int)\n# TODO: df['class_target_2'] = (df['mfe_percent'] > 1).astype(int)\n# TODO: is_long = df['signal_x'].astype(str).str.upper() == 'LONG'\n# TODO: df['total_mae'] = np.where(is_long, df['max_move_down_pct'].astype(float), df['max_move_up_pct'].astype(float))\n# TODO: df['class_target_3_corrected'] = (df['total_mae'] > 1.0).astype(int)\n# TODO: df['class_target_bad'] = ((df['total_mae'] > 1.0) & (df['pnl_percent'] < 0.1)).astype(int)\n\n# --- Regression targets (raw columns; transform applied inside cv_regression per REG_TARGETS) ---\n# TODO: df['target_profit'], df['target_quality'], df['target_danger'], df['target_entry'], df['target_exit']\n# TODO: REG_TARGETS = {\n#     'profit':       ('target_profit',  'log1p'),\n#     'quality':      ('target_quality', 'log5p'),\n#     'danger':       ('target_danger',  'log1p'),\n#     'entry_timing': ('target_entry',   'log1p'),\n#     'exit_timing':  ('target_exit',    'log1p'),\n# }\nREG_TARGETS = {}\n\n# TODO: print LONG/SHORT positive rate for all four classification targets -- every time\n# targets are (re)applied, not just the first time.\n","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"id":"3c57b91e-8868-4bd2-babd-a61b8d8e83e8","cell_type":"markdown","source":"### A.7 — Feature engineering pipeline (unchanged, leak-free, `FE_` prefix)\nAnalytics outcome columns (`mfe_percent`, `mae_percent`, `pnl_percent`, `trade_duration`, `exit_price`) are post-signal — only valid as lag-1 features. `WRAPPER_FIRST_FINAL_LONG`/`SHORT` still contains the dead reference `'FE_mfe_mae_ratio_lag'` — filter defensively (`[f for f in LIST if f in df.columns]`) or it will `KeyError`.","metadata":{}},{"id":"5b965a83-df75-4409-92f5-be87aace0e34","cell_type":"code","source":"# TODO: carry forward all FE_ engineered features from Week 7 unchanged.\n# TODO: confirm WRAPPER_FIRST_FINAL_LONG / SHORT are filtered defensively wherever used:\n#       [f for f in WRAPPER_FIRST_FINAL_LONG if f in df.columns]\n","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"id":"02ab7026-e633-40d6-9e28-741045a48aba","cell_type":"markdown","source":"### A.8 — Feature sets","metadata":{}},{"id":"9fb9a1ae-dbf2-4657-b354-c7b0ed1d9774","cell_type":"code","source":"# TODO: df_long, df_short split + sort by checked_at_utc\n# TODO: feat_set_long, feat_set_short = filtered FEATURES_COMBINED per side\n# TODO: print counts for FEATURES_ALL / FEATURES_COMBINED / df_long / df_short\n","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"id":"0d12f86a-293b-431b-97e5-6d48e3cd4335","cell_type":"markdown","source":"### A.9 — Walk-forward CV framework (finalized — `cv_no_scaling`/`cv_regression` are what tree ensembles use)\nTree-based models are scale-invariant, so `cv_no_scaling()` applies to `LGBMClassifier`/`LGBMRegressor` exactly as it did to RF and XGBoost. `cv_regression()` now takes a **string** transform key (`'log1p'`/`'log5p'`/absent) — this is the Week 7-end version, not the Week 5/6 boolean version. `'rmse'` is genuinely `sqrt(MSE)`, fixed at the source since Week 6.","metadata":{}},{"id":"7630aeac-cbbf-459e-a0a2-3d0de5a59772","cell_type":"code","source":"from sklearn.model_selection import TimeSeriesSplit\nfrom sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\nfrom sklearn.metrics import (\n    accuracy_score, precision_score, recall_score, f1_score, roc_auc_score,\n    mean_squared_error, mean_absolute_error, r2_score\n)\nfrom sklearn.base import clone\n\n# TODO: paste cv_with_scaling(), cv_no_scaling(), cv_regression() unchanged from Week 7's\n# closing version. cv_regression's signature: target_info = (target_col, transform),\n# transform in {'log1p', 'log5p', None}. Do NOT reintroduce the boolean version.\n\ndef cv_with_scaling(model, df_subset, feature_cols, target_col, n_splits=5, gap=0):\n    pass  # TODO\n\ndef cv_no_scaling(model, df_subset, feature_cols, target_col, n_splits=5, gap=0):\n    pass  # TODO\n\ndef cv_regression(model, df_subset, feature_cols, target_info, n_splits=5, gap=0, scale=False, clip_bounds=None):\n    pass  # TODO\n","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"id":"38fc6294-c15f-4473-9f90-9ef7321a8f9d","cell_type":"markdown","source":"### A.10 — Persistent results/model saving\n**Non-negotiable, per the session prompt and Week 7's own recurrence of this exact bug:**\n`RESULTS_DIR` and `save_result_dict` are defined ONCE, right here. No cell below this one --\nnot a tuning sweep, not a leaderboard cell, not anything pasted from Week 7 -- may reassign\n`RESULTS_DIR` to a bare relative path or redefine `save_result_dict` locally.","metadata":{}},{"id":"a0cf0675-4f31-46e6-9ccf-484c01cb8acb","cell_type":"code","source":"import os\nimport time\nimport json as _json\nimport subprocess as _sp\n\n# --- Identity / repo config -------------------------------------------------\nGITHUB_USERNAME = \"Jeshurun-B\"\nREPO_NAME       = \"EMA-optimizer-pipeline-v2\"\nUSER_EMAIL      = \"israelbajulaye@student.oauife.edu.ng\"\nPARENT_DIR      = os.getcwd()\nREPO_PATH       = os.path.join(PARENT_DIR, REPO_NAME)\n\n# Pull the token from Kaggle Secrets. Do this HERE, not inside save_progress(),\n# so a missing/misconfigured secret fails loudly at setup time -- not silently\n# three cells later when you're mid-experiment and don't notice the print.\nfrom kaggle_secrets import UserSecretsClient\nGITHUB_TOKEN = UserSecretsClient().get_secret(\"GITHUB_TOKEN\")\n\n\ndef _ensure_repo():\n    \"\"\"\n    Make sure REPO_PATH exists locally (clone if not), and return True/False.\n    Pulled out of save_progress() so it can run ONCE, up front, before anything\n    else (like RESULTS_DIR/MODELS_DIR) assumes the repo is there.\n    Does NOT chdir anywhere permanently -- caller decides cwd.\n    \"\"\"\n    if os.path.exists(REPO_PATH):\n        return True\n    remote_url = f\"https://{GITHUB_USERNAME}:{GITHUB_TOKEN}@github.com/{GITHUB_USERNAME}/{REPO_NAME}.git\"\n    print(f\"[_ensure_repo] Repository not found locally. Cloning {REPO_NAME}...\")\n    os.chdir(PARENT_DIR)\n    clone_result = _sp.run([\"git\", \"clone\", remote_url], capture_output=True, text=True)\n    if clone_result.returncode != 0:\n        print(\"[_ensure_repo] Clone failed:\")\n        print(_scrub(clone_result.stderr, GITHUB_TOKEN))\n        return False\n    print(\"[_ensure_repo] Clone complete.\")\n    return True\n\n\ndef _scrub(text, token):\n    \"\"\"Strip the PAT out of any git output before printing -- a failed clone/pull/push\n    can otherwise echo the token straight into notebook output.\"\"\"\n    return text.replace(token, \"***\") if token else text\n\n\n# --- Guarantee the repo exists BEFORE building any path that assumes it does ---\nif not GITHUB_TOKEN:\n    raise RuntimeError(\"[setup] GITHUB_TOKEN secret is missing -- fix this before continuing.\")\nif not _ensure_repo():\n    raise RuntimeError(\"[setup] Could not clone repo -- see error above.\")\n\n# --- NOW it's safe to build these as absolute paths INSIDE the repo, and to\n# create them. Previously RESULTS_DIR was a bare relative string created at\n# whatever cwd happened to be at import time -- which was often NOT inside\n# REPO_PATH, so files saved there lived outside the repo and never got pushed.\nRF_RESULTS_DIR   = os.path.join(REPO_PATH, \"Week_6_results\")\nRF_MODELS_DIR    = os.path.join(REPO_PATH, \"Rf_W6models\")\nXGB_RESULTS_DIR  = os.path.join(REPO_PATH, \"Week_7_results\")\nXGB_MODELS_DIR   = os.path.join(REPO_PATH, \"XGB-wk_7_models\")\nRESULTS_DIR      = os.path.join(REPO_PATH, \"Week_8_results\")   # this week's writes go here ONLY\nMODELS_DIR       = os.path.join(REPO_PATH, \"LGBM-wk_8_models\")\n\n\nos.makedirs(RF_RESULTS_DIR, exist_ok=True)\nos.makedirs(RF_MODELS_DIR, exist_ok=True)\nos.makedirs(XGB_RESULTS_DIR, exist_ok=True)\nos.makedirs(XGB_MODELS_DIR, exist_ok=True)\nos.makedirs(RESULTS_DIR, exist_ok=True)\nos.makedirs(MODELS_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n\ndef save_result_dict(d, name):\n    path = os.path.join(RESULTS_DIR, f\"{name}.json\")\n    with open(path, \"w\") as f:\n        _json.dump(d, f, indent=2, default=str)\n    return path\n\n\ndef save_model(model, name):\n    import joblib\n    path = os.path.join(MODELS_DIR, f\"{name}.joblib\")\n    joblib.dump(model, path)\n    return path\n\n\ndef save_progress(commit_message=None):\n    \"\"\"\n    Stage, commit, pull (merge), and push everything in REPO_PATH to GitHub.\n    Call this yourself after finishing a chunk of work -- not on autopilot.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not GITHUB_TOKEN:\n        print(\"[save_progress] Aborted: GITHUB_TOKEN is missing.\")\n        return False\n\n    if not _ensure_repo():\n        return False\n\n    os.chdir(REPO_PATH)\n\n    # --- Lock file: never auto-delete. A crashed prior git process leaves this\n    # behind, but a genuinely-running one does too -- can't tell the difference\n    # from here, so surface it as an error and let a human check. ---\n    lock_file = os.path.join(REPO_PATH, \".git\", \"index.lock\")\n    if os.path.exists(lock_file):\n        raise RuntimeError(\n            f\"[save_progress] {lock_file} exists. A git process may genuinely be \"\n            \"running, or a previous one crashed. Check manually before proceeding -- \"\n            \"deleting this blindly can corrupt the repo.\"\n        )\n\n    # --- Stage & commit local changes FIRST, before any pull/merge. This is what\n    # protects this session's work: once it's a local commit, a merge can only\n    # add to it, never silently lose it. ---\n    status = _sp.run([\"git\", \"status\", \"--porcelain\"], capture_output=True, text=True)\n    committed_something = False\n    if status.stdout.strip():\n        print(\"[save_progress] Changes to be committed:\")\n        print(status.stdout)\n        _sp.run([\"git\", \"add\", \".\"], check=True)\n        msg = commit_message or f\"Manual save: {time.strftime('%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S')}\"\n        _sp.run([\"git\", \"commit\", \"-m\", msg], check=True)\n        committed_something = True\n    else:\n        print(\"[save_progress] No local changes to commit.\")\n\n    # --- Pull with merge (--no-rebase) via \"origin\" (set once at clone time) so\n    # origin/main is actually updated -- the ahead-check below depends on that. ---\n    print(\"[save_progress] Pulling latest from origin/main to check for divergence...\")\n    pull_result = _sp.run(\n        [\"git\", \"pull\", \"origin\", \"main\", \"--no-rebase\"],\n        capture_output=True, text=True\n    )\n    print(\"PULL STDOUT:\", pull_result.stdout)\n\n    if pull_result.returncode != 0:\n        conflict_check = _sp.run(\n            [\"git\", \"diff\", \"--name-only\", \"--diff-filter=U\"],\n            capture_output=True, text=True\n        )\n        if conflict_check.stdout.strip():\n            print(\"[save_progress] MERGE CONFLICT -- stopping here, not resolving automatically.\")\n            print(\"Conflicted files:\\n\" + conflict_check.stdout)\n            print(\"Resolve manually (edit files, `git add <file>`, `git commit`), \"\n                  \"then call save_progress() again to push.\")\n            return False\n        else:\n            print(\"[save_progress] Pull failed for a non-conflict reason:\")\n            print(_scrub(pull_result.stderr, GITHUB_TOKEN))\n            return False\n\n    if \"up to date\" not in pull_result.stdout.lower() and \"up-to-date\" not in pull_result.stdout.lower():\n        print(\"[save_progress] Merged remote changes from another environment (e.g. Colab/Kaggle).\")\n\n    ahead_check = _sp.run(\n        [\"git\", \"rev-list\", \"--count\", \"origin/main..HEAD\"],\n        capture_output=True, text=True\n    )\n    commits_ahead = ahead_check.stdout.strip()\n    if commits_ahead == \"0\" and not committed_something:\n        print(\"[save_progress] Nothing new to push -- already in sync with origin/main.\")\n        return True\n\n    push_result = _sp.run([\"git\", \"push\", \"origin\", \"main\"], capture_output=True, text=True)\n    if push_result.returncode != 0:\n        print(\"[save_progress] Push failed:\")\n        print(_scrub(push_result.stderr, GITHUB_TOKEN))\n        return False\n\n\n\n    print(f\"[save_progress] Successfully pushed to GitHub at {time.strftime('%H:%M:%S')}\")\n    return True\n\nprint(\"done\")","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"id":"4befa419-c3fb-4fcf-974f-c2c6dc8efc22","cell_type":"markdown","source":"### A.11 — First task this week, not a side note: the RF-vs-XGBoost tally Week 7 never compiled","metadata":{}},{"id":"3ff7a178-02ba-4237-a1f9-cbba6610946b","cell_type":"code","source":"# TODO: load week8_baselines_to_beat.json (XGBoost's final numbers, saved at Week 7 close-out)\n#       AND week7_baselines_to_beat.json (RF's numbers) from PREV_RESULTS_DIR.\n# TODO: for all 18 target/direction combos (4 classification x2 directions = 8, 5 regression x2 = 10),\n#       compute win/loss: does XGBoost's saved number actually beat RF's saved number, combo by combo?\n# TODO: print an explicit count, e.g. \"XGBoost beats RF on X/18 combos\" -- mirroring how Week 6\n#       reported \"RF beats baseline 8/10\". Do not eyeball this from memory of last week's printouts --\n#       Week 7's own leaderboard cells manually re-typed remembered numbers more than once, which is\n#       exactly the failure mode this tally exists to avoid repeating.\n# TODO: specifically confirm: does the saved class_target_2 / class_target_3_corrected baseline\n#       actually reflect Week 3/4 LogReg's number (the thing RF lost to), or RF's own (weaker) number?\n#       Week 7's narrative assumed the former without re-checking the saved JSON value directly.\nrf_vs_xgb_tally = {}\n","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"id":"85df7ee0-7c4d-4f3e-80d0-4ad617c77cc0","cell_type":"markdown","source":"---","metadata":{}},{"id":"ed5cd2a9-c803-4f50-af68-0e6c107d573d","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## PART B — LightGBM Theory + Implementation (Monday)","metadata":{}},{"id":"554b8cd1-9d37-4a70-8cd3-eda39ab64a9c","cell_type":"markdown","source":"**Concept:** LightGBM grows trees **leaf-wise** (best-loss-reduction leaf split next) rather than **level-wise** (every leaf at a depth splits before moving deeper, XGBoost's default). Leaf-wise can reach a lower loss with fewer splits, but it's easier to overfit on a small/noisy leaf if `num_leaves`/`min_data_in_leaf` aren't controlled — think about which of your Week 6/7 depth findings (shallow depth generally best, `min_samples_leaf` interacting with depth) this predicts for LightGBM's own controls.\n\n**Histogram binning:** continuous features are pre-bucketed into a fixed number of histogram bins before split-finding, which is why LightGBM is typically faster on large tabular datasets than XGBoost's exact or approximate split search.","metadata":{}},{"id":"00707e69-f848-4f2c-9073-ba6717f446a9","cell_type":"markdown","source":"### Deliverable — Leaf-wise vs level-wise, in your own words (fill in)","metadata":{}},{"id":"9517bec7-c764-43fd-90b4-11433bfd293e","cell_type":"markdown","source":"*(your notes here — specifically: given Week 6/7's finding that shallow trees win on this dataset, what does that predict about how tightly you'll need to constrain `num_leaves` here?)*","metadata":{}},{"id":"1a1adec7-1691-4590-afd2-c745af98b65d","cell_type":"markdown","source":"### Train LGBMClassifier / LGBMRegressor with early stopping","metadata":{}},{"id":"8b567553-51b7-4bf2-9b55-76cd01108427","cell_type":"code","source":"# ============================================================\n# TODO: Train LGBMClassifier with early stopping, per classification target\n# ============================================================\n# TODO: mirror Week 7's XGBoost early-stopping pattern: split a genuine walk-forward\n#       validation fold distinct from the final CV test folds, fit with early_stopping,\n#       then evaluate the resulting n_estimators via cv_no_scaling() for comparability.\n# TODO: watch the off-by-one from Week 7 -- confirm whether best_iteration needs +1\n#       for the number of trees you actually want (Week 7's classifier loop and\n#       regressor loop disagreed on this; pick one convention and use it consistently\n#       across BOTH classification and regression this week).\nlgbm_clf_results = {}\n","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"id":"bdce4db8-21f2-4441-8117-a915e4e892bb","cell_type":"code","source":"# ============================================================\n# TODO: Train LGBMRegressor with early stopping, per REG_TARGETS\n# ============================================================\n# TODO: mirror the classifier loop above for all five REG_TARGETS, both directions.\n# TODO: use the STRING transform key ('log1p'/'log5p') from REG_TARGETS directly --\n#       do not reintroduce a boolean is_log flag.\nlgbm_reg_results = {}\n","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"id":"b51d900d-4ca0-42f8-ae7d-a0dc0180ebba","cell_type":"markdown","source":"### Tune: `num_leaves`, `min_data_in_leaf`, `learning_rate`, `bagging_fraction` (joint sweep)","metadata":{}},{"id":"12af79c2-7c4c-4aae-a5d4-9dbede893e6c