es stacking surface something non-obvious?\n","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"id":"aa0ff2b0-f89e-40c9-9a89-c07f90b1b5b4","cell_type":"markdown","source":"### Try different meta-models: LogReg vs Ridge vs another RF","metadata":{}},{"id":"02143fe6-c768-4c52-a02f-94bfa83bd091","cell_type":"code","source":"# TODO: swap final_estimator and re-run the same comparison -- does the choice of\n#       meta-model actually change the ranking, or just the margin?\n","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"id":"71138638-b695-461e-9336-a82573d6fad5","cell_type":"markdown","source":"### Calibration: reliability diagram — are confidence scores well-calibrated?","metadata":{}},{"id":"58b169ed-7ea2-427a-9ba2-5cf13397b523","cell_type":"code","source":"# TODO: from sklearn.calibration import calibration_curve\n# TODO: plot predicted-probability bins against observed positive rate, for your current\n#       best model AND the stacked ensemble\n","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"id":"ca04cc3e-bec2-4468-a885-5887dce32e23","cell_type":"markdown","source":"### Full model comparison — every model, same walk-forward folds\nSeparate classification and regression tables. Include training time and an interpretability note (e.g. \"single coefficient vector\", \"SHAP available\", \"meta-model over 4 base learners\") for each row -- not just the metric.","metadata":{}},{"id":"e38f311e-5c52-4614-b888-b5c525b74df6","cell_type":"code","source":"# TODO: classification_comparison = pd.DataFrame([...])  -- rows: LogReg, DecisionTree, RF,\n#       XGBoost, LightGBM, Stacked -- columns: target, direction, AUC, train_time_s, notes\n# TODO: regression_comparison = pd.DataFrame([...])  -- same models, R2 instead of AUC\n# TODO: shortlist top 2-3 models to carry forward toward Week 9 (SVM) and eventual deployment\nclassification_comparison = None\nregression_comparison = None\n","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"id":"4fe95475-e41a-4418-b2